# robo.vn - a layered character with a bone rig: robo.psd has +folders for the head and both arms (each forearm in a
# folder of its own), so rig.json hangs the hand on the forearm, the forearm on the arm and the arm on the spine.
# Nothing jumps here: put the cursor on the `label robo_demo:` line and use Preview from cursor (Ctrl+Enter).
# Open the character in the animation studio (Animate in the Files panel) and switch to Rig mode to see the bones.

define robo "Robo" color=#7cc4ff

label robo_demo:
  scene bg_park_evening fade 0.5
  show robo cheerful at center fade 0.4
  robo: Hello! I am drawn in a PSD with +folders, so I have bones: a spine, a neck, a head, and two arms with a forearm each. #uggm
  animate robo wave
  robo: Waving moves the arm, and the forearm swings on top of it, because it hangs from the arm. #oxcf
  animate robo nod
  robo: A nod turns the head and the neck, and the antenna wobbles about a pivot of its own. #j9le
  show robo calm
  animate robo shrug
  robo: Both arms and the head move in one animation. #i618
  show robo cheerful
  animate robo dance
  robo: Everything at once: the whole body bounces on the root bone. #un70
  show robo pose=salute
  robo: Parameters drive the arm and the head from sliders; a pose is a saved set of them. # #gljn
  animate robo lookaround
  robo: And an animation can key them: this one only turns the head, with no keys on a bone. # #fza3
  hide robo fade 0.4
